) traps heat in the atmosphere, leading to the warming of the Earth''s surface.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', 'cf0d08c74cc91724ad52db16180224348678d7ba8a6c522be5624dfd9a152ee7');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'In which stage of a river do ox-bow lakes typically form?', '["Youthful stage","Middle stage","Old stage","Torrential stage"]', 2, 'Ox-bow lakes form in the old (lower) stage of a river when a meander is cut off through deposition.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', 'eaecb2e81e1bf28f74b82d34058b5dfbff5366578163aa483fafe9b25129df8e');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The primary source of energy for the Earth is the _____.', '["Moon","Sun","Stars","Core"]', 1, 'The Sun provides solar radiation, which is the fundamental source of energy for the Earth''s climate and life.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '7603281d522bb3eed2685a7063f0da81abc5ac3a44d962a584661860660f1eac');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The leading producer of Petroleum in Africa is _____.', '["Egypt","Nigeria","South Africa","Kenya"]', 1, 'Nigeria is historically the largest producer of petroleum in Africa, although output fluctuates.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '474741574945101e80252cfae678ce7fdc0c90c8823d1f50bc9eba97d51f4788');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'A linear settlement pattern is most likely to develop along a _____.', '["Lake","Road","Market","Hilltop"]', 1, 'Linear settlements form in a line, often following a transport route such as a road, railway, or river.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '001c2108d8d37764f4b23b5d06fecd48aac54f550981fc6ba0b190a792ba60e0');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The term ''Albedo'' refers to the _____.', '["Heat absorbed by the earth","Reflectivity of a surface","Total solar output","Thickness of the ozone"]', 1, 'Albedo is the fraction of solar energy reflected from the Earth back into space.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '8ccd14345cc91fa9ca00806a25d1c38ecd79ec523512577827d49a27f0be96e9');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'Which of the following is a landlocked country in West Africa?', '["Senegal","Liberia","Mali","Ghana"]', 2, 'Mali is entirely surrounded by land and has no direct access to the sea.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '4e44a0523f0838781a36892d5b6c0892f27f349568b48ccfb70ffc9370dbc781');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The transition zone between the Sahara desert and the Savannah is the _____.', '["Veld","Sahel","Prairies","Steppe"]', 1, 'The Sahel is the semiarid region of Western and North-Central Africa forming a transition between the Sahara to the north and the Sudanian Savanna to the south.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '17b15120751103932229f20d47a208800f63d7be2387aca0e57cf5d45f56e4e9');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'Which type of rock is formed from pre-existing rocks under great heat and pressure?', '["Igneous","Sedimentary","Metamorphic","Basalt"]', 2, 'Metamorphic rocks are formed when igneous or sedimentary rocks are subjected to high heat and pressure without melting.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '6964cf869dc9580e023d7f07572a096a5b3c1d35c940f8565bd2d9d43a4d5e8a');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The instrument used to measure wind direction is the _____.', '["Anemometer","Wind Vane","Hygrometer","Barometer"]', 1, 'A wind vane (or weather cock) points in the direction from which the wind is blowing.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '77c005ba3a2e1d44afbf42aa66ed935b5c942520770d452a1d2002ed274791bb');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'A rejuvenated river is one that has _____.', '["Dried up","Reached the sea","Gained new erosive power","Stopped flowing"]', 2, 'River rejuvenation occurs when a river''s vertical erosive power is increased, usually due to a fall in sea level or rise in land.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '4493c2f58ae3683f5d526b1d63d767d178ac83d180493ee24b1eea8202389b1f');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'Which of the following is an example of an intrusive igneous rock?', '["Basalt","Obsidian","Granite","Pumice"]', 2, 'Granite forms from magma that cools slowly deep underground, making it an intrusive (plutonic) igneous rock.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', 'f081be7dfa07f6bcd9b88dadf2b6ad3f41154c113e1492f65898f444034acb7f');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The ''Great Rift Valley'' is a major feature of _____.', '["West Africa","East Africa","North Africa","Southern Africa"]', 1, 'The Great Rift Valley is a continuous geographic trench running through Ethiopia, Kenya, and Tanzania.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', 'e4c594d9cde26b859d61513e71b4139b3dbe4d055e45bae9d4054601a47fba91');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'The process by which plants release water vapor through their leaves is _____.', '["Evaporation","Condensation","Transpiration","Precipitation"]', 2, 'Transpiration is the biological process where water is taken up by roots and released into the atmosphere as vapor through leaf stomata.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', '9a2e37a3f2bc7e43c43956050e98a1c31f8b3254b90053229e551ac43aa93097');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (exam, subject, year, topic, q_text, options_json, answer_idx, explanation, passage, source_file, hash) VALUES ('NECO', 'Geography', 2024, NULL, 'A plateau that drops steeply to the surrounding lowlands is a/an _____.', '["Escarpment","Cuesta","Inselberg","Ridge"]', 0, 'An escarpment is a steep slope or long cliff that forms as a result of erosion or faulting and separates two relatively level areas.', NULL, 'NECO_Geography_2024.json', 'cd90d3bfb7a2b8e6ec63375dc8b47dc35840a426c3cf73ceba7cfb4fc17eab7a');
